Upstream work
-------------

WardenOne builds on filter lists and filtering techniques from the wider
ad-blocking and privacy community. Sources are identified in CREDITS.md, and
their copyright and attribution rights are retained.

THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.html and licenses/ accompany both extension profiles.
Settings → About WardenOne opens the packaged notices without a network request.
Third-party material retains its own terms; WardenOne's GPL does not relicense
all upstream data. In particular rules-adshield.json and rules-easyprivacy.json
are adaptations of EasyList/EasyPrivacy under CC BY-SA 3.0:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/
They contain selected, converted and supplemented rules; modification notice
recorded 2026-10-19. Other list-specific notices identify the applicable terms.

The corresponding cosmetic filter source, retaining original headers and
full-input/source-subset SHA-256 identifiers, is in
docs/filter-source-snapshot.json.gz in the public source repository. Unused
network records are omitted. tools/build-cosmetics.js --from-snapshot rebuilds the packaged
artifact from those inputs. The same source tree includes the source-form
rules, adapters, MPL-covered list material and build scripts. A distributor
must keep that corresponding source available alongside its build:
https://github.com/iri-dev/WardenOne

Four configured feeds have specific scope exceptions documented in
docs/source-rights-review.md. Written permissions for Phishing Army and
flinteger remain granted; those exceptions concern identified upstream inputs.
